{{> cloudflare/production-url-section publicUse="the Payload config, the sitemap and the preview links read"}}

### First deploy

From the repository root, once the steps above are done. The first deploy of a Worker takes its secrets from a file: the Worker does not exist yet, so `wrangler secret put` cannot run.

{{#orderedSteps}}
{{#step}}
Give the build the production URL, as a shell variable (it wins over `.env`). Next.js freezes `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` into the bundle, and Payload takes its server URL and the origins it trusts from it:

   ```bash
   export NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://{{projectName}}-web.<subdomain>.workers.dev
   ```
{{/step}}
{{#step}}
Write the secrets of the web Worker to a file (gitignored):

   ```bash
   printf 'PAYLOAD_SECRET=%s\nPREVIEW_SECRET=%s\n' "$(openssl rand -base64 32)" "$(openssl rand -base64 32)" > apps/web/.prod.env
   ```
{{/step}}
{{#step}}
Build the web Worker, then deploy it with the secrets file and delete the file: the Worker holds the secrets now.

   ```bash
   {{#inDirectory "apps" "web"}}{{runScript "build:cf"}}{{/inDirectory}}
   {{#inDirectory "apps" "web"}}{{runScript "deploy" "--secrets-file .prod.env"}}{{/inDirectory}}
   rm apps/web/.prod.env
   ```

   `build:cf` bundles every `.env*` value of the app into the Worker as a fallback for a secret that was never set, so build where `apps/web/.env` holds no real secret (CI, or a checkout without a `.env`). Later deploys are `{{#inDirectory "apps" "web"}}{{runScript "build:cf"}}{{/inDirectory}}` and `{{#inDirectory "apps" "web"}}{{runScript "deploy"}}{{/inDirectory}}`.
{{/step}}
{{#step}}
Deploy the cron Worker with its token, the same way. Its daily schedule is registered on deploy.

   ```bash
   printf 'BACKUP_TRIGGER_TOKEN=%s\n' "$(openssl rand -base64 32)" > apps/cron/.prod.env
   {{#inDirectory "apps" "cron"}}{{runScript "deploy" "--secrets-file .prod.env"}}{{/inDirectory}}
   rm apps/cron/.prod.env
   ```
{{/step}}
{{#step}}
Check the site, with a retry: routes answer 404 for about a minute after `wrangler deploy`.

   ```bash
   for i in $(seq 1 12); do curl -fsS -o /dev/null "$NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL/" && break; sleep 10; done
   ```
{{/step}}
{{/orderedSteps}}
